  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to the manufacture of\nseasonal and decorative lighting products containing lead; and to repeal\nsection 1376-b of the public health law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S7889",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7889-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §1376-b, Pub Health L (as proposed in S.5675-A & A.4522-A); add Art 25-C §389-s, ren §399-g to be §389-t, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7889\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to the manufacture\nof seasonal and decorative lighting products containing lead; and to\nrepeal section 1376-b of the public health law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.634, to move language to General Business Law, clarifies the responsi-\nble entities for any violations, and adjusts the penalty amount for\nviolations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter to create a new article\nunder General Business Law specifically for products containing lead and\nclarifies that the new statute will apply to products distributed after\nthe effective date. The legislation also clarifies that manufacturers\nwill ultimately be responsible for any violations due to their role in\nthe supply chain. The legislation also sets the civil penalty at five\nhundred dollars per violation.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 634 of the Laws of 2021. S.1201A and\nA.4662A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in May 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending the public health law relating to\nthe manufacture and sale of seasonal and decorative lighting products\ncontaining lead, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.  5675-A and\nA. 4522-A, takes effect.\n",
